    "notes": {
        "174973b0-5e1f-4368-872b-821c18d3866d": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 432,
            "width": 736,
            "height": 320,
            "content": "## Test data assumption: one real Nuki device\n\nNuki has no sandbox. The connected account (API token with the scopes smartlock.readOnly, smartlock.action, smartlock.auth and smartlock.log) must hold at least one Smart Lock that is online. The flow takes the first device Find Smartlocks returns, so no device ID is hardcoded.\n\nThe flow creates the account user **test+nuki-e2e@appmixer.ai** and Nuki e-mails an app invitation to that address on every run. Both the authorization and the account user are deleted at the end. If a run is aborted, delete the account user in Nuki Web first: Nuki rejects a second account user with the same e-mail address.\n\nCreate App Invite waits until Nuki Web lists the new authorization (up to 5 minutes), so the After All timeout is 480 s. The \"notConfirmed\" port is left open on purpose: when the authorization never appears the flow times out and fails."
        }
    }
}
